Style
  ASCII / CRT Terminal style from the lemo-opuscar film-style library
  (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT for code · CC BY 4.0 for style docs).
  crt.js (monochrome phosphor CRT pass) is copied from the style's demo under the MIT licence; the glyph engine
  (term.js), timeline, score and foley were written for this film.

Puzzle and numbers
  The puzzle was generated for this film (tools/pick.js) and has exactly one solution.
  Solve time, tries and step-backs were measured with solver.js on this machine (see FACTS.md).

Voice
  Typecast text-to-speech (typecast.ai), voice "Jinhee" (ssfm-v30), generated with the account connected to this session.
  Check Typecast's terms for your plan before publishing commercially.

Music and sound
  Original analogue-synth score synthesised in code (score.py: PolyBLEP oscillators, ladder filter, reverb).
  All foley synthesised in code (mix.py; compressor and limiter from lemo-opuscar core/audio/sfx.py).
  No samples or recordings are used.

